    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate leaning heavily on **Junior Caminero** (73.35) and **Yordan Alvarez** (68.01) as our primary anchors. **Junior Caminero** benefits from a massive 19% SP skill boost against Chris Bassitt, overcoming a park factor drag to maintain the highest efficiency score in our lineup. Meanwhile, **Yordan Alvarez** remains a locked-in start despite facing George Kirby; his elite xwOBA of .464 and favorable platoon alignment ensure his production floor remains high enough to anchor the outfield. **Caleb Durbin** (62.34) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (61.57) provide our highest potential for stolen bases, with **Caleb Durbin** specifically benefiting from a favorable SP skill rating and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** enjoying the leadoff spot against Matthew Liberatore, despite the inherent risk of a platoon disadvantage.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved **Chase Meidroth** (36.88), who fell just shy of our 40.0 efficiency threshold for a start against Jobe. While **Chase Meidroth** enjoyed a park boost, the 17% SP skill penalty\u2014combined with a neutral platoon outlook and a lower-order lineup placement\u2014resulted in a sub-floor projection that necessitates benching him to preserve our limited game caps. We are also monitoring several lineup-pending statuses, most notably **Gary Sanchez** and **Christian Yelich**, both of whom are projected to face Yoshinobu Yamamoto. While **Gary Sanchez** is currently flagged for a marginal score of 47.75, his utility is bolstered by a wind-out advantage that provides a slight cushion against Yamamoto\u2019s 3.61 xERA. **Christian Yelich** offers a higher floor (58.98) due to a robust dynamic platoon advantage, though we must keep a close eye on the official confirmation to ensure he isn't rested against the tough right-handed opposition.",
